+# Sepet End-to-End Audit
+
+## 1. Module map
+
+| Python module | Responsibilities | Tables read | Tables written |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `sepet/api/db.py` | Opens the SQLite connection, supplies UTC timestamps, hashes and verifies passwords with salted PBKDF2. The connection sets `row_factory` but does not enable foreign keys (`sepet/api/db.py:11-14`). | None directly. | None directly. |
+| `sepet/api/auth.py` | Resolves Bearer tokens, enforces authentication, and returns role/profile tuples for customer, restaurant, and courier guards (`sepet/api/auth.py:18-60`). | `auth_token`, `"user"` (`sepet/api/auth.py:10-15`); `restaurant` (`sepet/api/auth.py:42-45`); `courier` (`sepet/api/auth.py:54-57`). | None. |
+| `sepet/api/accounts.py` | Registers customers/restaurants, logs users in, returns the current user, and tops up customer wallets (`sepet/api/accounts.py:59-123`). | `"user"` during registration/login (`sepet/api/accounts.py:63-64`, `92-95`); indirectly `auth_token` and `"user"` through auth. | `"user"` (`sepet/api/accounts.py:65-68`, `116-119`); `restaurant` (`sepet/api/accounts.py:70-84`); `auth_token` (`sepet/api/accounts.py:50-56`). |
+| `sepet/api/main.py` | Hosts FastAPI, mounts routers, lists restaurants/cuisines, exposes restaurant details, order creation, and a public order detail endpoint (`sepet/api/main.py:13-17`, `33-214`). | `restaurant` and `restaurant_review` (`sepet/api/main.py:44-54`); `restaurant`, `menu_item`, `restaurant_review`, `"user"` (`sepet/api/main.py:85-115`); `"order"`, `restaurant`, `order_item` (`sepet/api/main.py:121-136`); `restaurant`, `menu_item` (`sepet/api/main.py:150-161`). | `"user"` for balance deduction (`sepet/api/main.py:181-184`); `"order"` (`sepet/api/main.py:189-203`); `order_item` (`sepet/api/main.py:205-212`). |
+| `sepet/api/panels.py` | Provides customer history, restaurant operations, courier creation/assignment, courier delivery, delivery confirmation, and earnings reporting (`sepet/api/panels.py:68-272`). | `"order"` with `restaurant`, `"user"`, and `courier` (`sepet/api/panels.py:52-81`, `90-102`, `194-203`); `courier` (`sepet/api/panels.py:110-113`, `176-179`); `menu_item` (`sepet/api/panels.py:121-124`); aggregate `"order"` earnings (`sepet/api/panels.py:251-263`). | `"user"` and `courier` for courier creation (`sepet/api/panels.py:134-144`); `menu_item` (`sepet/api/panels.py:151-156`); `"order"` for assignment/delivery/confirmation (`sepet/api/panels.py:182-185`, `219-222`, `237-240`). |
+| `sepet/api/reviews.py` | Computes displayed restaurant ratings and creates one review per approved customer order (`sepet/api/reviews.py:13-50`). | `restaurant` (`sepet/api/reviews.py:27-29`); `"order"` (`sepet/api/reviews.py:32-36`); `restaurant_review` (`sepet/api/reviews.py:39-42`). | `restaurant_review` (`sepet/api/reviews.py:44-49`). |
+| `sepet/api/seed.py` | Deletes the database, recreates all tables, inserts demo restaurants, menu items, users, and courier profiles (`sepet/api/seed.py:162-230`). | `restaurant` while resolving inserted IDs (`sepet/api/seed.py:200-203`). | All tables through schema creation and seed inserts: `restaurant`, `menu_item`, `"user"`, `courier` (`sepet/api/seed.py:164-227`). |
+
+## 2. Coupling
+
+All runtime coupling is direct Python imports plus FastAPI's dependency injection:
+
+- `accounts.py -> auth.py`: imports `get_current_user` for `/api/auth/me` and wallet authorization (`sepet/api/accounts.py:7`, `102`, `111`).
+- `accounts.py -> db.py`: imports the connection helper and password/time utilities (`sepet/api/accounts.py:8`); used at `sepet/api/accounts.py:62`, `67`, `91`, `95`, `54`.
+- `auth.py -> db.py`: imports `get_db` for every token/profile lookup (`sepet/api/auth.py:3`, `19`, `42`, `54`).
+- `main.py -> accounts.py`: imports and mounts `accounts_router` (`sepet/api/main.py:7`, `15`).
+- `main.py -> auth.py`: imports optional authentication and customer authorization (`sepet/api/main.py:8`); used at `sepet/api/main.py:83`, `143`.
+- `main.py -> db.py`: imports `get_db` for all main-router queries and order writes (`sepet/api/main.py:9`, `47`, `84`, `121`, `149`).
+- `main.py -> panels.py`: imports and mounts `panels_router` (`sepet/api/main.py:10`, `16`).
+- `main.py -> reviews.py`: imports the shared rating function and review router (`sepet/api/main.py:11`, `17`); rating coupling is active at `sepet/api/main.py:59-61` and `103`.
+- `panels.py -> auth.py`: imports all three role guards (`sepet/api/panels.py:6`); they gate every panel endpoint (`sepet/api/panels.py:68-272`).
+- `panels.py -> db.py`: imports connection, password hashing, and timestamp utilities (`sepet/api/panels.py:7`); used across panel routes (`sepet/api/panels.py:70`, `101`, `109`, `120`, `133`, `151`, `168`, `193`, `211`, `229`, `250`).
+- `reviews.py -> auth.py`: imports optional/customer auth and `require_customer` (`sepet/api/reviews.py:5`, `22`).
+- `reviews.py -> db.py`: imports `get_db` and timestamp helper (`sepet/api/reviews.py:6`, `26`, `48`).
+- `reviews.py -> panels.py`: imports the request model `ReviewInput`, creating a data-contract coupling between routers (`sepet/api/reviews.py:7`, `20-22`).
+- `seed.py -> db.py`: imports password hashing and timestamp generation (`sepet/api/seed.py:4`, `193-194`).
+
+There is also implicit coupling on status strings. `main.py`, `schema.sql`, `panels.py`, and `reviews.py` each independently encode `hazırlanıyor` or `onaylandı` (`sepet/api/main.py:109`, `199`, `214`; `sepet/api/schema.sql:60`; `sepet/api/panels.py:174`, `238`; `sepet/api/reviews.py:34`). The current bytes inspected are the same correct Unicode sequence, but the duplication remains a correctness hazard.
+
+## 3. Request lifecycle
+
+Authentication paths share this chain: route dependency -> `get_current_user` (`sepet/api/auth.py:23-26`) -> `resolve_user` (`sepet/api/auth.py:18-20`) -> `_user_from_token` (`sepet/api/auth.py:6-15`) -> `db.get_db` (`sepet/api/db.py:11-14`) -> `auth_token JOIN "user"`. Role guards then may open a second connection for the restaurant or courier profile (`sepet/api/auth.py:42-48`, `54-60`).
+
+| Method and endpoint | Lifecycle from route handler to database and back |
+|---|---|
+| `POST /api/auth/register` | `register` validates email/role/required restaurant fields (`sepet/api/accounts.py:59-61`, `35-47`) -> `get_db` -> checks `"user"` by email (`sepet/api/accounts.py:63-64`) -> inserts `"user"` (`65-68`) -> optionally inserts `restaurant` (`70-84`) -> `issue_token` inserts `auth_token` (`50-56`, `85`) -> transaction commit and token/user response (`86`). |
+| `POST /api/auth/login` | `login` -> `get_db` -> selects `"user"` by email (`sepet/api/accounts.py:91-94`) -> `verify_password` (`95`, implemented `sepet/api/db.py:27-33`) -> `issue_token` inserts `auth_token` (`sepet/api/accounts.py:97`) -> returns token and `user_payload` (`98`, `31-32`). |
+| `GET /api/auth/me` | `me` -> auth dependency chain (`sepet/api/accounts.py:101-103`) -> `_user_from_token` joins `auth_token` with `"user"` (`sepet/api/auth.py:10-15`) -> `user_payload` returns id/email/role/balance (`sepet/api/accounts.py:31-32`). |
+| `POST /api/auth/wallet/topup` | `top_up_wallet` -> auth dependency chain (`sepet/api/accounts.py:110-115`) -> verifies customer role (`112-113`) -> `get_db` -> `UPDATE "user"` balance (`116-119`) -> reselects balance (`122`) -> returns new balance (`123`). |
+| `GET /api/restaurants` | `list_restaurants` -> `get_db` -> selects `restaurant` with optional search conditions (`sepet/api/main.py:33-48`) -> aggregates `restaurant_review` (`49-54`) -> converts rows and calls `displayed_rating` (`55-62`, function `sepet/api/reviews.py:13-15`) -> Python filtering and sorting (`sepet/api/main.py:63-70`). |
+| `GET /api/cuisines` | `list_cuisines` -> `get_db` -> `SELECT DISTINCT cuisine FROM restaurant` (`sepet/api/main.py:73-79`). |
+| `GET /api/restaurants/{restaurant_id}` | `get_restaurant` -> optional auth dependency (`83`) -> `get_db` -> selects `restaurant` (`85-89`), `menu_item` (`90-93`), and `restaurant_review JOIN "user"` (`94-99`) -> builds response and computes displayed rating (`100-105`) -> if authenticated customer, reuses connection to check approved `"order"` and existing `restaurant_review` (`106-115`) -> returns restaurant/menu/review payload (`116`). |
+| `GET /api/orders/{order_id}` | `get_order` has no auth dependency (`sepet/api/main.py:119-120`) -> `get_db` -> selects `"order" JOIN restaurant` (`122-128`) -> selects `order_item` (`131-136`) -> returns all order columns plus items and restaurant name (`137-139`). |
+| `POST /api/orders` | `create_order` -> `require_customer` auth chain (`143`) -> validates non-empty items (`144-147`) -> `get_db` -> selects `restaurant` (`150-154`) -> selects matching `menu_item` rows (`156-164`) -> computes subtotal/min order/total (`166-174`) -> checks and atomically deducts `"user"` balance (`181-186`) -> inserts `"order"` (`189-203`) and one or more `order_item` rows (`205-212`) -> returns id/status/total (`214`). |
+| `GET /api/orders/history` | `order_history` -> `require_customer` (`sepet/api/panels.py:68-69`) -> `get_db` -> selects the customer's `"order"` rows joined to `restaurant`, `"user"`, and `courier` (`70-80`) -> `serialize_orders` runs one `order_item` query per order (`35-48`, `81`). |
+| `GET /api/restaurant/orders` | `restaurant_orders` -> `require_restaurant` resolves user and `restaurant` profile (`87`, `sepet/api/auth.py:39-48`) -> filters by status if supplied (`sepet/api/panels.py:86-100`) -> `get_db` -> selects this restaurant's orders with joins (`90-103`) -> `serialize_orders` loads items (`35-48`). |
+| `GET /api/restaurant/couriers` | `list_couriers` -> `require_restaurant` (`106-108`) -> `get_db` -> selects `courier` rows for the restaurant (`109-114`). |
+| `GET /api/restaurant/menu-items` | `list_menu_items` -> `require_restaurant` (`117-119`) -> `get_db` -> selects `menu_item` for the restaurant (`120-125`). |
+| `POST /api/restaurant/couriers` | `create_courier` -> `require_restaurant` (`128-130`) -> checks name and email uniqueness (`131-135`) -> `get_db` -> inserts `"user"` as courier (`136-139`) -> inserts `courier` profile (`141-144`) -> returns created courier (`145`). |
+| `POST /api/restaurant/menu-items` | `add_menu_item` -> `require_restaurant` (`148-150`) -> `get_db` -> inserts `menu_item` (`151-156`) -> returns generated ID and payload (`157`). |
+| `POST /api/restaurant/orders/{order_id}/assign-courier` | `assign_courier` -> `require_restaurant` (`160-166`) -> `get_db` -> selects `"order"` (`169-171`) -> checks restaurant ownership and `hazırlanıyor` status (`172-175`) -> selects the restaurant-owned `courier` (`176-181`) -> updates `"order"` courier/time/status to `kuryede` (`182-186`) -> returns status/name (`187`). |
+| `GET /api/courier/orders` | `courier_orders` -> `require_courier` resolves user and courier profile (`190-192`, `sepet/api/auth.py:51-60`) -> `get_db` -> selects `"order"` rows assigned to that courier (`sepet/api/panels.py:193-203`) -> `serialize_orders` loads items (`204`). |
+| `POST /api/courier/orders/{order_id}/deliver` | `deliver_order` -> `require_courier` (`207-209`) -> `get_db` -> selects `"order"` (`212-214`) -> checks assignment and `kuryede` status (`215-218`) -> updates status/time to `teslim_edildi` (`219-222`) -> returns status (`223`). |
+| `POST /api/orders/{order_id}/confirm_delivery` | `confirm_delivery` -> `require_customer` (`226-227`) -> `get_db` -> selects `"order"` (`230-232`) -> checks ownership and `teslim_edildi` status (`233-236`) -> updates status/time to `onaylandı` (`237-240`) -> returns status (`241`). |
+| `GET /api/restaurant/earnings` | `restaurant_earnings` -> `require_restaurant` (`247-249`) -> `get_db` -> runs overall and confirmed aggregate queries on `"order"` (`251-263`) -> computes pending revenue and averages in Python (`264-272`). |
+| `POST /api/restaurants/{restaurant_id}/reviews` | `create_review` -> `require_customer` (`sepet/api/reviews.py:18-23`) -> validates comment (`24-25`) -> `get_db` -> checks `restaurant` (`27-31`), approved `"order"` (`32-38`), and duplicate `restaurant_review` (`39-43`) -> inserts `restaurant_review` (`44-49`) -> returns created review (`50`). |
+
+## 4. Data model
+
+`sepet/api/schema.sql` defines seven application tables plus tokens. There are no explicit indexes beyond uniqueness constraints.
+
+| Table | Columns and constraints | Endpoints that touch it |
+|---|---|---|
+| `restaurant` | `id` PK autoincrement, `name`, `cuisine`, `rating`, `delivery_fee`, `min_order`, `eta_minutes`, `image_emoji`, nullable `user_id` FK to `"user"` (`sepet/api/schema.sql:1-11`). | `POST /api/auth/register` (`sepet/api/accounts.py:70-84`); restaurant list/detail (`sepet/api/main.py:44-87`); order creation (`150-151`); restaurant role lookup (`sepet/api/auth.py:42-45`); restaurant panel routes (`sepet/api/panels.py:106-157`); review creation (`sepet/api/reviews.py:27-31`); seeding (`sepet/api/seed.py:167-182`, `211-214`). |
+| `"user"` | `id` PK autoincrement, unique `email`, `password_hash`, role constrained to customer/restaurant/courier, `balance` default 0 (`sepet/api/schema.sql:13-19`). | Register/login/me/topup (`sepet/api/accounts.py:63-123`); auth token lookup (`sepet/api/auth.py:10-15`); order balance deduction (`sepet/api/main.py:181-184`); order/restaurant joins (`sepet/api/main.py:94-99`, `sepet/api/panels.py:72-77`, `194-200`); courier creation (`sepet/api/panels.py:134-140`); seeding (`sepet/api/seed.py:195-219`). |
+| `auth_token` | `token` PK, `user_id` FK, `created_at`; no expiry column (`sepet/api/schema.sql:21-25`). | `POST /api/auth/register` and `/login` insert tokens (`sepet/api/accounts.py:50-56`, `85`, `97`); every authenticated route reads it through `sepet/api/auth.py:10-15`. |
+| `courier` | `id` PK autoincrement, unique `user_id` FK, required `restaurant_id` FK, `name` (`sepet/api/schema.sql:27-32`). | Courier role lookup (`sepet/api/auth.py:54-60`); courier list/create/assignment (`sepet/api/panels.py:106-187`); courier order queries (`190-204`); order joins (`72-77`, `90-102`); order courier FK (`sepet/api/schema.sql:63`); seeding (`sepet/api/seed.py:215-227`). |
+| `restaurant_review` | `id` PK autoincrement, `restaurant_id` and `user_id` FKs, rating check 1-5, `comment`, `created_at`, unique pair (`sepet/api/schema.sql:34-42`). | Restaurant list/detail ratings (`sepet/api/main.py:49-62`, `94-115`); review creation (`sepet/api/reviews.py:39-49`). |
+| `menu_item` | `id` PK autoincrement, `restaurant_id` FK, `name`, `description`, `price`, `category` (`sepet/api/schema.sql:44-51`). | Restaurant detail (`sepet/api/main.py:90-93`); order creation price lookup (`156-164`); restaurant menu list/add (`sepet/api/panels.py:117-157`); seeding (`sepet/api/seed.py:183-191`). |
+| `"order"` | `id` PK autoincrement, `restaurant_id` FK, `address`, `phone`, `note`, `total`, `status`, `created_at`, nullable `customer_id` and `courier_id` FKs, assignment/delivery/confirmation timestamps (`sepet/api/schema.sql:53-67`). | Order creation (`sepet/api/main.py:189-203`); public order detail (`119-139`); history/panel/assignment/delivery/confirmation/earnings (`sepet/api/panels.py:68-241`, `251-263`); approved-order checks (`sepet/api/main.py:106-111`, `sepet/api/reviews.py:32-36`). |
+| `order_item` | `id` PK autoincrement, `order_id` and `menu_item_id` FKs, denormalized `name`, `unit_price`, `quantity` (`sepet/api/schema.sql:69-76`). | Order creation (`sepet/api/main.py:205-212`); all order serialization (`sepet/api/main.py:131-136`, `sepet/api/panels.py:35-48`). |
+
+## 5. Risks: the ten most serious issues
+
+1. **Public order endpoint exposes private delivery data.** `GET /api/orders/{order_id}` has no dependency and no ownership check; it returns the entire `"order"` row, including `address`, `phone`, and `note`, for any sequential integer ID (`sepet/api/main.py:119-139`). Concrete fix: require `get_current_user`, and allow only the owning customer or the restaurant/courier legitimately attached to that order; return a narrowed schema rather than `o.*`.
+2. **Tokens never expire and logout is client-side only.** `auth_token` stores only creation time (`sepet/api/schema.sql:21-25`), token lookup has no TTL (`sepet/api/auth.py:6-15`), issuing creates another token on every login (`sepet/api/accounts.py:50-56`), and frontend logout only removes localStorage (`web/src/AuthContext.tsx:56-59`). Concrete fix: add `expires_at`, enforce it in `_user_from_token`, add a server-side logout delete, and clean up old tokens.
+3. **Foreign keys are declared but not enforced by the API.** Tables have FK constraints (`sepet/api/schema.sql:10`, `23`, `29-30`, `35-37`, `45`, `55`, `62-63`, `70-72`), but every API connection is opened without `PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON` (`sepet/api/db.py:11-14`). Concrete fix: make `get_db()` a closing context manager and execute the pragma before returning each connection; do the same for seed connections.
+4. **All money is floating point.** Restaurant fees/minima/ratings, balances, totals, and item prices are `REAL` (`sepet/api/schema.sql:5-7`, `18`, `49`, `59`, `74`). Order totals are computed and rounded with Python floats (`sepet/api/main.py:166-174`), making cumulative and comparison errors possible. Concrete fix: store integer kuruş, parse/serialize as Decimal, and make wallet/order arithmetic integer-based.
+5. **Courier assignment has a check-then-update race and no busy check.** `assign_courier` selects the order, then later updates it without repeating the status condition in SQL (`sepet/api/panels.py:169-186`). Two concurrent assignments can both pass the check and overwrite each other; the same courier can also receive unlimited concurrent orders. Concrete fix: use a conditional update (`WHERE id = ? AND restaurant_id = ? AND status = ?`) with `rowcount`, add a unique/incomplete-assignment policy, and run order/courier checks in one explicit transaction.
+6. **Role profiles can be ambiguous and ownership assumptions are implicit.** `restaurant.user_id` is not unique (`sepet/api/schema.sql:10`) while `require_restaurant` uses `fetchone` and returns the first match (`sepet/api/auth.py:42-48`). A malformed or externally modified database could make the selected restaurant arbitrary. Concrete fix: add `UNIQUE` to `restaurant.user_id`, or explicitly select one owned restaurant and reject duplicates; likewise assert `courier.user_id` uniqueness remains protected.
+7. **Database connections are not explicitly closed.** `get_db()` returns a raw connection (`sepet/api/db.py:11-14`), and SQLite's connection context manager commits/rolls back but does not close it. Several routes continue using `conn` after `with` exits, so the code depends on garbage collection: restaurant review checks (`sepet/api/main.py:106-115`) and history serialization (`sepet/api/panels.py:70-81`). Concrete fix: expose `get_db()` with `@contextmanager` and `try/finally: conn.close()`, or close explicitly after serialization.
+8. **Restaurant registration accepts unsafe economic and operational values.** `delivery_fee`, `min_order`, and `eta_minutes` are plain numbers (`sepet/api/accounts.py:18-22`), while validation only checks role/name/cuisine (`40-47`). A restaurant account can be created with negative fees, negative minimum orders, or negative ETA and then be used in order calculations (`sepet/api/main.py:166-174`). Concrete fix: apply Pydantic `Field(ge=...)`/upper bounds to fees/min order and `Field(gt=0)` to ETA; reject non-finite values.
+9. **Order contact and review payloads have almost no server-side bounds.** Address, phone, and note are arbitrary strings (`sepet/api/main.py:25-30`); the frontend checks only display-level constraints (`web/src/pages/Checkout.tsx:35-43`). Menu/review models also permit empty/oversized text (`sepet/api/panels.py:19-32`, `sepet/api/reviews.py:24-25`). Concrete fix: enforce address/note length limits, normalize/validate phone server-side, require non-empty menu fields, and cap comment length.
+10. **Courier account creation is under-validated.** `CourierInput` accepts arbitrary email/password/name (`sepet/api/panels.py:13-16`); only nonempty name is checked (`131-132`). No email format, password length, or nonempty password rule exists, unlike customer/restaurant registration (`sepet/api/accounts.py:35-47`). Concrete fix: reuse email/password validation, apply minimum password length, and return proper conflict errors for duplicate users.
+
+Additional lower-ranked observations: order statuses are duplicated strings with no SQL `CHECK` (`sepet/api/schema.sql:60`; `sepet/api/panels.py:174`, `220`, `238`); duplicate-email race can return a 500 instead of 409 (`sepet/api/accounts.py:63-68`); API queries have no pagination (`sepet/api/panels.py:70-81`, `90-103`, `193-204`); localStorage token storage increases XSS impact (`web/src/AuthContext.tsx:41-43`); and the demo credentials are intentionally public in the UI (`web/src/pages/Account.tsx:77-82`).
+
+## 6. Frontend
+
+The client is a React Router SPA. `main.tsx` mounts providers in the order Auth -> Cart -> App (`web/src/main.tsx:9-18`), and all routes are registered in `App.tsx` (`web/src/App.tsx:47-54`). API access is centralized in `web/src/api.ts`: a single `request<T>` helper reads the token from localStorage, sets a Bearer header, sends JSON when a body exists, and extracts FastAPI's `detail` on error (`web/src/api.ts:3-21`). Vite proxies all `/api` calls to the FastAPI server at `127.0.0.1:8000` during development (`web/vite.config.ts:6-10`).
+
+Principal flows:
+
+- Authentication stores both token and user in `sepet-auth`; startup calls `/api/auth/me` when a token exists (`web/src/AuthContext.tsx:17-39`, `41-44`). Registration/login are called from `Account.tsx` (`web/src/pages/Account.tsx:14-26`, `54-68`).
+- Customer shopping fetches restaurants/filters (`web/src/api.ts:32-47`; `web/src/pages/Restaurants.tsx:24-42`) and restaurant detail/menu/reviews (`web/src/api.ts:44-45`; `web/src/pages/RestaurantDetail.tsx:18-27`).
+- The cart is persisted to `sepet-cart-v1` and stores full `MenuItem` objects plus a client-side delivery fee (`web/src/CartContext.tsx:21-33`). Checkout posts only IDs and quantities to the backend (`web/src/api.ts:51-67`; `web/src/pages/Checkout.tsx:46-50`).
+- Customer wallet/history uses `/api/auth/wallet/topup`, `/api/orders/history`, and confirmation (`web/src/api.ts:83-85`, `117-121`; `web/src/panels/CustomerPanel.tsx:23-49`, `105-109`).
+- Restaurant and courier panels call order, menu, courier, earnings, assignment, and delivery endpoints (`web/src/api.ts:87-123`; `web/src/panels/RestaurantPanel.tsx:25-46`; `web/src/panels/CourierPanel.tsx:10-23`).
+
+Where frontend and backend disagree:
+
+- **Order data exposure is wider than the UI expects.** `OrderPage` renders private address/phone/note (`web/src/pages/OrderPage.tsx:34-38`) and the type models them as normal fields (`web/src/types.ts:34-47`), but the backend exposes these unauthenticated to anyone with the ID (`sepet/api/main.py:119-139`).
+- **Delivery-fee trust differs.** The client can display a fee from route state or stale cart data (`web/src/pages/Checkout.tsx:14`, `20`), while the server recalculates the authoritative fee from `restaurant.delivery_fee` (`sepet/api/main.py:166-174`). The server is safe, but the displayed total can disagree until submission.
+- **Balance is stale immediately after ordering.** The backend deducts balance inside order creation (`sepet/api/main.py:181-184`), but `Checkout` only clears the cart and navigates; it never calls `refreshUser` (`web/src/pages/Checkout.tsx:46-54`). The header/checkout can keep showing the pre-order balance.
+- **Auth requirements are UI-first rather than route-guarded.** `/checkout` is publicly reachable and only disables submission without a user (`web/src/pages/Checkout.tsx:64-76`); the backend does enforce `require_customer` (`sepet/api/main.py:142-147`). The same applies to `/panel`, which renders a login prompt (`web/src/pages/Panel.tsx:7-19`).
+- **Error handling is inconsistent.** Restaurant panel mutations and review submission `await` requests without local try/catch (`web/src/panels/RestaurantPanel.tsx:132-174`; `web/src/pages/RestaurantDetail.tsx:101-110`), so failures can produce unhandled promise rejections. Customer confirmation similarly does not catch errors (`web/src/panels/CustomerPanel.tsx:33-36`).
+- **Status presentation diverges.** Customer and restaurant panels map four localized statuses (`web/src/panels/CustomerPanel.tsx:7-12`; `web/src/panels/RestaurantPanel.tsx:10-15`), but CourierPanel displays the raw status (`web/src/panels/CourierPanel.tsx:35`). The API has no status enum/schema (`sepet/api/schema.sql:60`).
+- **Cart identity is keyed only by restaurant ID.** `CartContext.add` starts a new cart when IDs differ (`web/src/CartContext.tsx:35-48`) and RestaurantDetail asks the user before clearing (`web/src/pages/RestaurantDetail.tsx:39-46`), but stale persisted menu objects/fees are not revalidated against the API (`web/src/CartContext.tsx:21-33`).
+- **Client validation is not authoritative.** Phone/address/min order/balance checks are visual or submit-time (`web/src/pages/Checkout.tsx:33-43`, `74`, `92-96`; `web/src/pages/RestaurantDetail.tsx:154-158`); the backend currently repeats only min order and balance, not address/phone shape (`sepet/api/main.py:166-186`).
+

